US_MAP tests; enum value tests | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` | Role: test | Connection: all readiness tests use COMPLETE/DEFERRED/SKIPPED; no FAILED coverage; new downstream-skip test required | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_query.py` | Role: test | Connection: `update_status` tests do not cover FAILED; readiness tests depend on terminal status semantics | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` | Role: test | Connection: conformance tests for all backends; FAILED status behavior must be covered for all three | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` | Role: test | Connection: only tests COMPLETE path; FAILED exit path is unverified | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Status Values table, `sam state` valid values, Field Ownership Rules \u2014 all become stale | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: SAM state machine diagram missing `failed` node; readiness rule prose omits FAILED; \u00a72.1a status output schema incomplete | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Progress Loop termination and SubagentStop hook description become inaccurate | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Completion Verification Gate terminal-status check does not account for FAILED | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Step 7 completion instruction does not mention FAILED or failure handling | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: terminal status understanding used in dependency correctness dimension | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py::ItemStatus` | Role: other-reference | Connection: already has `FAILED`; no code change needed but naming collision requires documentation clarity | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 root source of `TERMINAL_STATUSES`; the split into `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` / `TERMINAL_STATUSES` must be done correctly or all three backends and the dependency graph engine produce wrong readiness and blocked-task results simultaneously\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` and `memory.py` \u2014 both import `TERMINAL_STATUSES` and use it for dependency satisfaction; if the split is not applied here, FAILED parents will incorrectly unblock downstream tasks\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 the SubagentStop handler is the only automatic trigger for FAILED status; without the FAILED branch, the entire feature is inert; and without calling `mark_downstream_skipped` from this path, downstream tasks remain permanently unblocked\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` \u2014 `test_all_members_count` will fail immediately after the enum change; CI will be red until this is patched\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility: `TERMINAL_STATUSES` is imported by 3 backends and `implementation_manager.py` with different semantics needs; the split into SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES (for dependency satisfaction) vs TERMINAL_STATUSES (for cycle/readiness checks) must be propagated consistently\\n  - verification: zero test coverage for FAILED status, downstream-skip behavior, and the SubagentStop FAILED branch\\n  - documentation: the SAM state machine diagram, TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md, and multiple skill/agent instructions enumerate the 6-value status set without FAILED\\n  - behavioral: `backlog_core/operations.py::_SAM_TERMINAL_STATUSES` and `implementation_manager.py::_TERMINAL_STATUSES` are independent copies that will diverge silently if not updated\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `backlog_core/operations.py::_SAM_TERMINAL_STATUSES` \u2014 not in the original item description; a third independent TERMINAL_STATUSES implementation used by `get_ready_sam_tasks` (MCP-level dispatch readiness query)\\n  - `implementation_manager.py::_TERMINAL_STATUSES` \u2014 not in the original item description; a fourth independent copy for the legacy implementation manager dispatch loop\\n  - `dispatch_schema/core/models.py::ItemStatus.FAILED` \u2014 already defined at this layer; creates a naming ambiguity that needs documentation treatment\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Concerns\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n#### Rationale\\n\\nThe proposed addition of `TaskStatus.FAILED` with automatic downstream skipping aligns precisely with the product mission and established design principles:\\n\\n**Alignment with Plugin Identity and Process Ownership**\\n\\nThe development harness is designed to \\\"provide a reusable, language-independent development workflow based on the Stateless Agent Methodology (SAM)\\\" ([CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md:11-12)). The proposed change enhances the SAM task state machine \u2014 a core process artifact \u2014 by adding the `failed` terminal status to represent a canonical failure outcome. This is a process-level concern (orchestrator dispatch, dependency graph readiness) not a language-specific concern, placing it squarely within the harness's responsibility domain.\\n\\n**Alignment with Design Principle: Every Stage Produces MCP-Registered Artifact**\\n\\nThe design principle states: \\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact (stateless handoff) \u2014 stored via `artifact_register` and retrieved via `artifact_read`, never via direct filesystem paths\\\" ([CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md:16)). The proposed change operates at the SAM task schema level (`models.py::TaskStatus`, `dependencies.py::TERMINAL_STATUSES`, `dependencies.py::DependencyGraph`) \u2014 all code-level data structures that are internal to the MCP servers. It does not introduce filesystem paths or artifact management changes. The downstream-skip marker is written via the standard `sam_task(action='state', status='failed')` MCP call, consistent with existing artifact handling patterns.\\n\\n**Alignment with Design Principle: Human Escalation Follows ARL**\\n\\nThe design principle states: \\\"Human escalation follows ARL constraint analysis, not arbitrary checkpoints\\\" ([CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md:17)). The proposed change makes task failure handling automatic \u2014 the `mark_downstream_skipped` method executes without human intervention when a parent task enters `failed` status. This removes an arbitrary manual step (having a human operator manually mark downstream tasks as skipped) and replaces it with deterministic, constraint-derived behavior. Tasks depending on a failed parent are inherently unsatisfiable (the dependency cannot be met if the upstream task failed), so automatic skipping is a direct consequence of ARL constraint analysis: the downstream task's constraint \\\"parent must complete successfully\\\" cannot be satisfied, triggering auto-skip.\\n\\n**Alignment with SAM 7-Stage Pipeline Architecture**\\n\\nThe harness defines the SAM task state machine in `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` (lines 306-316), which currently shows six status values. The proposed change adds a seventh terminal status (`failed`) to the state machine. This is a documented extension point \u2014 the SM diagram explicitly lists terminal statuses as \\\"complete, deferred, skipped\\\" in the readiness rule (line 318). Adding `failed` as a seventh terminal status for the purpose of representing explicit failures (as opposed to deferred or skipped, which have different semantics) aligns with the documented state machine and extends it in the expected direction.\\n\\n**Alignment with Historical Direction**\\n\\nRecent merged PR #1871 (commit 3e06aa1, 2026-04-21) added `Plan.autonomy` field to the SAM schema to control dispatch-time gating behavior. That change modified `models.py` with a new enum field (`autonomy: str = Field(default=\\\"full_auto\\\", ...)`) and updated `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and `workflow-architecture-diagram.md` to reflect the change. The proposed `TaskStatus.FAILED` change follows the same pattern:\\n1. Extend the `TaskStatus` StrEnum with a new member\\n2. Update `TERMINAL_STATUSES` constant (requires careful split between `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` for dependency satisfaction vs `TERMINAL_STATUSES` for cycle detection)\\n3. Update all consumer code that imports `TERMINAL_STATUSES`\\n4. Update documentation files (`TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, `workflow-architecture-diagram.md`)\\n5. Update test expectations\\n6. Wire new behavior into the hook (`task_status_hook.py`)\\n\\nThis is a well-established pattern in the codebase.\\n\\n**Alignment with Composition Model: Harness Owns Process**\\n\\nThe composition model states: \\\"The harness owns the *process*; language plugins own the *specialists*\\\" ([CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md:174-187)). The proposed change modifies process-level orchestration (task status representation, dependency graph readiness rules, DAG walking for downstream skip) \u2014 all owned by the harness, not by language plugins. Language plugins do not define task statuses; they use the harness-provided task format. This change is entirely within the harness's scope.\\n\\n#### Evidence from Product Sources\\n\\n- **Source**: CLAUDE.md, lines 11-19 (Plugin Identity and Design Principles)\\n- **Source**: docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md, lines 306-318 (SAM Task State Lifecycle, terminal status definition)\\n- **Source**: docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md (Status Values table \u2014 currently lists 6 values; extension to 7 is consistent with StrEnum pattern)\\n- **Source**: Merged PR #1871 (commit 3e06aa1, 2026-04-21) \u2014 historical precedent for SAM schema extension with coordinated updates to models, docs, tests, and hooks\\n- **Source**: Item's own RT-ICA and Fact-Check sections establish that the change is derivable from available code and has zero missing information (all 9 conditions are AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE)\\n\\n#### Potential Documentation Drift Signals\\n\\nThe proposed change requires synchronization of four documentation sources (currently out of sync by design, pre-update):\\n1. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 Status Values table (lines 309-316)\\n2. `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 SAM state machine diagram (lines 306-316) and readiness rule prose (line 318)\\n3. `agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 Step 7 completion instruction\\n4. `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Progress Loop termination condition\\n\\nThese drift signals are expected and documented in the item's Impact Radius section. No new or undocumented dependencies emerged.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add taskstatus.failed with automatic downstream skipping on task failure** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/cursor-cookbook.md \u2014 pattern: Error Propagation / automatic downstream task skipping (DAG Task Runner)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-05)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a missing-feature item, not a regression. The absence is observable by inspection:\\n\\n1. Open `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` and verify `TaskStatus` has no `FAILED` member (lines 49\u201357).\\n2. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py -k \\\"failed\\\"` \u2014 expect zero test collection (no FAILED-path coverage exists).\\n3. Transition a task to any non-`complete`/`deferred`/`skipped` status and call `get_ready_tasks()` on a plan where that task is a dependency \u2014 observe the downstream task is never returned as ready and the plan makes no forward progress.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 P1 (should-have).\\n\\nA plan that contains a failing task halts silently: no forward progress, no diagnostics, no way for the orchestrator or human to distinguish a hung plan from an actively running one. The missing status directly impairs plan observability and causes wasted orchestrator cycles when humans must manually inspect and patch task state.\\n\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 adding a new `StrEnum` member touches a well-defined set of producers and consumers (see Files section). The blast radius is high but the change type is additive. The critical constraint is keeping two semantically distinct sets straight: a `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` set (for dependency satisfaction \u2014 COMPLETE, DEFERRED only) and an expanded `TERMINAL_STATUSES` set (for plan-completion checks \u2014 COMPLETE, DEFERRED, SKIPPED, FAILED).\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks plan completion**: A failed task that has no canonical terminal status keeps `TERMINAL_STATUSES` unsatisfied, so `get_ready_tasks()` never dispatches dependents. The plan appears stuck with no forward progress and no indication of why.\\n- **Misrepresents task history**: The only available workarounds \u2014 leaving the task `in-progress` or writing it as `skipped` \u2014 produce false plan state. `in-progress` implies the task is still running; `skipped` implies it was intentionally bypassed. Both corrupt the audit trail.\\n- **Bottleneck in orchestrator loop**: `implement-feature` and `implementation_manager.py` poll `get_ready_tasks()` or `TERMINAL_STATUSES`-gated checks (lines 121, 751). A plan with a stuck failed task causes infinite-wait or manual operator intervention on every poll cycle.\\n- **Parallel orphan downstream tasks**: Without auto-skipping, tasks downstream of a failed task remain `not-started` indefinitely. Operators cannot easily tell which tasks are orphaned vs. legitimately queued \u2014 especially in multi-wave milestone dispatch.\\n- **Status Map gap**: `STATUS_MAP` in `models.py` has no `failed` normalization entry, so any ad-hoc string written by an agent or human operator is silently dropped when the model is re-read.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Plan execution makes forward progress even when a task fails \u2014 downstream tasks are explicitly skipped rather than orphaned.\\n- Operators can distinguish between \\\"intentionally skipped\\\", \\\"failed and cascade-skipped\\\", \\\"deferred\\\", and \\\"complete\\\" without reading YAML comments or session logs.\\n- `get_ready_tasks()` returns a correct empty list for a plan where all remaining tasks are unreachable due to upstream failures \u2014 closing the infinite-wait loop.\\n- `implementation_manager.py status` and plan-completion checks gain an accurate terminal count, enabling correct plan-done detection.\\n- `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler can route a failed exit to the canonical `failed` status, making the GitHub sync reflect actual outcomes rather than silent `complete`.\\n- Resolves the blocked-state ambiguity for stalled-task detection (#1944): a `failed` task is distinct from an `in-progress` task that has gone silent.\\n- Unlocks correct dispatch-state recording via `dispatch_item_status(status='failed')` which already exists as a valid value in the dispatch schema but lacks a corresponding SAM status.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a task's execution fails and its status is set to `failed`:\\n\\n1. `failed` is a recognized member of `TaskStatus` and round-trips through YAML serialization without loss.\\n2. A task with status `failed` is treated as terminal for plan-completion purposes \u2014 it does not block plan-done detection.\\n3. A task with status `failed` does NOT satisfy dependency requirements. Tasks that depend solely on a `failed` task are not dispatched.\\n4. Tasks that depend solely on a `failed` parent are automatically transitioned to `skipped` with a reason referencing the upstream failure \u2014 they do not remain `not-started`.\\n5. `get_ready_tasks()` returns an empty list when all remaining `not-started` tasks have at least one upstream dependency in `failed` status.\\n6. The `STATUS_MAP` recognizes `\\\"failed\\\"` (and common variants such as `\\\"FAILED\\\"`, `\\\"error\\\"`) and normalizes them to `\\\"failed\\\"`.\\n7. Agent instructions, documentation, and the SAM state machine diagram reflect the new `failed` state and its cascade-skip behavior.\\n8. Existing plans with none of the six original statuses altered continue to operate identically \u2014 the change is fully additive from the perspective of existing valid plan files.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import TaskStatus; assert TaskStatus.FAILED == 'failed'\\\"` exits 0.\\n2. `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import STATUS_MAP; assert STATUS_MAP.get('FAILED') == 'failed' and STATUS_MAP.get('failed') == 'failed'\\\"` exits 0.\\n3. A plan YAML round-trip (write \u2192 read \u2192 write) with a task whose status is `failed` produces identical YAML with no data loss.\\n4. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py -k \\\"failed\\\"` collects and passes tests that verify `TaskStatus.FAILED` membership and `STATUS_MAP` normalization.\\n5. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py -k \\\"failed_status or downstream_skip\\\"` collects and passes: a test creating a 3-task chain T01\u2192T02\u2192T03, transitioning T01 to `failed`, and asserting T02 and T03 receive `status=skipped` with a reason containing \\\"T01\\\"; and a test asserting `get_ready_tasks()` returns `[]` for that plan.\\n6. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` continues to pass (no regression in the existing complete-path).\\n7. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/` exits 0 with no new failures across the full suite.\\n8. `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` Status Values table contains a `failed` row with a description distinguishing it from `skipped`.\\n9. `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` SAM state machine section shows `failed` as a terminal state with a downstream cascade-skip edge.\\n10. `grep -r \\\"FAILED\\\\|failed\\\" plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` shows the new member in both `TaskStatus` and `STATUS_MAP`.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `TaskStatus` enum and `STATUS_MAP` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 `TERMINAL_STATUSES`, `DependencyGraph` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 consumer at lines 175, 478 |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 consumer at lines 562, 596 |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop path |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 independent `_TERMINAL_STATUSES` copy |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 independent `_SAM_TERMINAL_STATUSES` copy |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` |\\n| Prior art | PR #1871 \u2014 SAM schema extension pattern (coordinated models/docs/tests/hooks updates) |\\n| Skill | `/dh:development-harness` \u2014 pipeline context |\\n| Skill | `/dh:planner-rt-ica` \u2014 RT-ICA framework used in grooming |\\n| Related item | #1944 \u2014 stalled-task detection (downstream benefit once FAILED exists) |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Core producers (status enum and terminal-set definitions):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `TaskStatus` (lines 49\u201357), `STATUS_MAP` (lines 25\u201346)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 `TERMINAL_STATUSES` (line 15), `DependencyGraph` (no `mark_downstream_skipped` method exists; must be added)\\n\\n**Core consumers (all import `TERMINAL_STATUSES` directly or shadow it):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 lines 175, 478\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 lines 562, 596\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 line 842 (hardcodes `SamTaskStatus.COMPLETE` \u2014 no FAILED branch)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 line 121 (independent `_TERMINAL_STATUSES` copy), line 751 (readiness check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 line 4057 (`_SAM_TERMINAL_STATUSES` independent copy), line 4087 (readiness check)\\n\\n**Tests requiring update or addition:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` \u2014 count assertion on `TaskStatus` members will break; add FAILED coverage\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` \u2014 no FAILED-path coverage; add downstream-skip tests\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` \u2014 add FAILED exit path test\\n\\n**Documentation requiring update:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 Status Values table\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 SAM state machine diagram\\n\\n**Agent instructions requiring update:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` (task-worker dispatch instructions)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 this item is self-contained. All source files exist and are readable. No external dependencies are required.\\n- Blocks (will be unblocked by this item):\\n  - #1944 (stalled-task detection via `LastActivity`) \u2014 can distinguish `failed` from legitimately `in-progress` tasks once `FAILED` is a canonical status\\n  - Any dispatch-state work that relies on `dispatch_item_status(status='failed')` being reflected in SAM task state\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 the enum addition itself is small, but the change touches 9 source files plus tests and docs across 3 distinct sub-packages (`sam_schema`, `backlog_core`, `implementation-manager`). The critical complexity is the `TERMINAL_STATUSES` split: the single frozenset must become two semantically distinct sets (one for dependency satisfaction, one for plan-completion), and 5 independent copies of the set across the codebase must all be updated consistently. Test coverage gaps in `test_dependencies.py` require new test cases before the feature can be verified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The TaskStatus enum lacks a FAILED value and TERMINAL_STATUSES does not include it. When a task execution fails, the system has no canonical way to represent \\\"failed and downstream should auto-skip\\\" \u2014 the design gap allows failed tasks to remain in-progress, blocking dependents indefinitely without explicit skip signals. A quality gate should enforce that terminal status transitions (especially failures) automatically propagate skip signals to the dependency DAG.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Failed task T01 \u2192 T02, T03 remain stuck waiting \u2192 **to** \u2192 Failed task T01 \u2192 T02, T03 auto-marked skipped with reason \\\"upstream T01 failed\\\" \u2192 plan progresses\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`TaskStatus` at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py:49-57` defines six values: `not-started`, `in-progress`, `complete`, `blocked`, `deferred`, `skipped`. There is no `failed` value. `TERMINAL_STATUSES` at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py:15` is `frozenset({COMPLETE, DEFERRED, SKIPPED})`. A task whose execution fails has no canonical destination status \u2014 the orchestrator either leaves it `in-progress` (then queries surface it as still active), marks it `blocked` (which is non-terminal, so dependents are not unblocked), or manually edits to `skipped` (which falsely signals \\\"intentionally skipped\\\"). Because no status can mean \\\"failed and downstream should not run\\\", `get_ready_tasks()` (`dependencies.py:67-92`) cannot tell a downstream task to auto-skip when its parent has failed. The agent for the dependent task will not be dispatched (parent never enters TERMINAL_STATUSES), but the plan also never makes forward progress and the dependents are not flagged as unreachable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`TaskStatus` adds a `FAILED = \\\"failed\\\"` value. `TERMINAL_STATUSES` is split into two sets:\\n\\n- `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES = frozenset({COMPLETE, DEFERRED})`\\n- `TERMINAL_STATUSES = frozenset({COMPLETE, DEFERRED, SKIPPED, FAILED})` (kept for cycle/readiness checks)\\n\\n`DependencyResolver` gains a `mark_downstream_skipped(failed_task_id: str) -> list[str]` method that walks the transitive dependents of a failed task, sets each to `SKIPPED` with a `reason` like \\\"skipped: upstream {task_id} failed\\\", and returns the list of newly-skipped task IDs. The `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler (or `sam_task(action='state', status='failed')`) calls this on transition to `failed`. `get_ready_tasks()` continues to require dependencies be in `SUCCESSFUL_STATUSES` \u2014 so an auto-skipped task is itself terminal and never dispatched.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun:\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run pytest plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/ -k \\\"failed_status or downstream_skip\\\"\\n```\\n\\nA test passes that creates a 3-task plan T01 -> T02 -> T03, transitions T01 to `failed`, calls the new resolver method, and asserts T02 and T03 both have `status=\\\"skipped\\\"` with `reason` containing \\\"upstream T01 failed\\\". A second assertion: `get_ready_tasks()` returns an empty list. The string `\\\"failed\\\"` appears in `TaskStatus` and `models.py` line range now contains a `FAILED = \\\"failed\\\"` member.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: `./research/agent-frameworks/cursor-cookbook.md` \u2014 DAG Task Runner pattern: \\\"Includes timeout protection, automatic downstream task skipping on parent failure, graceful signal handling\\\" (Key Features section, lines 89-90) and \\\"Error Propagation: Automatic downstream task skipping on parent failure prevents cascading failures and wasted computation\\\" (Patterns Worth Adopting #5, line 257).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f2b83f5dbfc57140e6cf8d77856d47c607c856c6b0d2796c4aa1b64afa1f35d7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCbMgw\"}"}